        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "77072aba-0907-5c22-a41a-64614631e725",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Marcel Duchamp, Jiang Wen, Lu Chuan, Ning Jing, Wu Yujuan\n- Works: Prelude to a Broken Arm, The Missing Gun\n- Roles: painter, sculptor, chess player, writer, film actor, screenwriter, director\n- Concepts: Cubism, conceptual art, Dada\n\nFacts:\n- Marcel Duchamp was born on 28 July 1887 and died on 2 October 1968.\n- Marcel Duchamp was a French-American painter, sculptor, chess player, and writer.\n- Marcel Duchamp's work was associated with Cubism, conceptual art, and Dada, but he was careful about using the term Dada and was not directly associated with Dada groups.\n- Jiang Wen was born on 5 January 1963 and is a Chinese film actor, screenwriter, and director.\n- Prelude to a Broken Arm is a 1915 sculpture by Marcel Duchamp.\n- Prelude to a Broken Arm consisted of a regular snow shovel with the title and the words \"from Marcel Duchamp 1915\" painted on the handle.\n- The Missing Gun is a 2002 Chinese black comedy film directed by Lu Chuan.\n- The Missing Gun stars Jiang Wen, Ning Jing, and Wu Yujuan.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
