        "text": "Page: Marcel Duchamp. Sentence: Henri-Robert-Marcel Duchamp (] ; 28 July 1887 – 2 October 1968) was a French-American painter, sculptor, chess player and writer whose work is associated with Cubism, conceptual art and Dada, although he was careful about his use of the term Dada and was not directly associated with Dada groups.\nPage: Jiang Wen. Sentence: Jiang Wen (born 5 January 1963) is a Chinese film actor, screenwriter, and director.\nPage: Prelude to a Broken Arm. Sentence: Prelude to a Broken Arm (En prévision du bras cassé in French) is a 1915 sculpture by Dada artist Marcel Duchamp that consisted of a regular snow shovel with the title and \"from Marcel Duchamp 1915\" painted on the handle.\nPage: The Missing Gun. Sentence: The Missing Gun () is a 2002 Chinese black comedy film directed by Lu Chuan and starring Jiang Wen, Ning Jing and Wu Yujuan.",
